  "id": "COMPOUND:295 - PROTEIN:5865",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that mitomycin may exert its biological effects on SK-VLB through a series of molecular interactions involving bromodomain-containing proteins and ubiquitin carboxyl-terminal hydrolases. Specifically, mitomycin is linked to bromodomain-containing protein 4 and ubiquitin carboxyl-terminal hydrolase 5, both of which are targets of palmarumycin CP18, which in turn targets SK-VLB. This indicates a potential pathway where mitomycin modulates the activity of these proteins, possibly through enzyme inhibition or regulatory mechanisms, which ultimately influence SK-VLB. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple overlapping targets and the involvement of ubiquitin-dependent pathways highlight the complexity of the interaction, and further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct role of mitomycin in SK-VLB regulation.",
